{"id": "EUVD-2026-103666", "enisaUuid": "b5b00fe8-0b0a-356f-9c72-64c14fba09cb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: gue: reject invalid REMCSUM offsets\n\nThe REMCSUM option carries an absolute checksum start and checksum field\noffset. gue_remcsum() passes them to skb_remcsum_process(), whose\npartial path stores offset - start in the u16 skb->csum_offset variable.\nIf offset is less than start, this underflows.\n\nA forwarded packet can retain CHECKSUM_PARTIAL and reach a NETIF_F_HW_CSUM\ndriver which trusts the metadata, leading skb_copy_and_csum_dev() to write\ntwo bytes about 64 KiB beyond the destination buffer.\n\nReject reversed tuples in validate_gue_flags(), after the existing length\nvalidation, so all GUE parsers enforce the ordering in one place.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b9bc21b2396c396d88dd909caaf73d5be6ff593", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43efb1f997e976f386aa89716f55870cd2cff9ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1eeec0c51fd5598da44080ed96bbd9880021c28b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d664be4ca49d1696e85239236f4988dfc4653c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97f907203321eee2cc9132d5c9eb47698fb41d35", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40aeafbcbc7bc4018e8f74bbbb4d29ed8846f57f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c20f755338ca234e523dfc943719f194dfc1f903", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2566866fc30965d915d0b52b5c3323b362619f0e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98621", "GHSA-2cjw-phmm-3745"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c99b0ea-e104-39b4-881c-a4160aa250a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <4b9bc21b2396c396d88dd909caaf73d5be6ff593"}, {"id": "2dc03063-3563-3897-a761-72bccf03490e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "42d8c530-8502-3960-892f-c01a35e33c7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "45e8d134-c7a2-3ed6-83f0-a4ddb423184e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "480dc41b-788d-3f6f-8072-ca6677555495", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "58e51567-34a4-3e4c-8366-7efccecfa80c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <1eeec0c51fd5598da44080ed96bbd9880021c28b"}, {"id": "67b5309e-7469-3e55-a4fc-d84f4ab1ca0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "9b374058-244e-3119-a1fe-403b918ac54a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <c20f755338ca234e523dfc943719f194dfc1f903"}, {"id": "a9d3d9c7-5dac-30f6-8a4e-e027fe846763", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b772d719-e4e7-3604-aae9-8d8fed4a0034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <40aeafbcbc7bc4018e8f74bbbb4d29ed8846f57f"}, {"id": "b8a31a75-435c-3887-a31e-0051fb0c1fdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "bd38588a-7cf4-3f8b-be40-421c77f9ef64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <2566866fc30965d915d0b52b5c3323b362619f0e"}, {"id": "c5fc3363-4973-3292-b54e-d65c48c3c61c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe881ef11cf0220f118816181930494d484c4883 <1d664be4ca49d1696e85239236f4988dfc4653c3"}, {"id": "cc2f1780-a611-3c5e-b71a-5879a2d95f42", "product": {"name": "Linux"